{
  "about": "The round_half_away_from_zero verb in a specification (FORMULA-16): what the check refuses before any study data is read, what a run reports for a source in a relation no input declares, and the rows a run gives when its source is qualified by its driver, read through a named intermediate, nested in a case result or derived in a row template. The document positive is the specification of the benchmark schema-round-half-away-from-zero-ties and adsl its input; negative is the specification of negative-round-half-away-from-zero-non-numeric-source, whose study data no case writes. A case that keeps the independent rows states the benchmark's authored expected/adsl.csv as its output, read with the declared types: STUDYID and USUBJID are str and VAL1, VAL0, RND1 and RND0 are float, an empty field missing; a rounded zero is positive zero (FORMULA-16). Moved from the declarative_rounding module of scalar_declarative_rounding.rs, whose tests compared the fields each case's compares names, the complete issue rows, or that a variant checks clean, builds without an issue and gives the table of that expected file.",
  "documents": {
    "positive": "yamaa: \"1.0\"\ntype: spec\nmodel: ADaM\ndomain: ADSL\nkeys: [STUDYID, USUBJID]\ninput:\n  SOURCE: input/adsl.csv\n\noutput:\n  path: adsl.csv\n  columns: [STUDYID, USUBJID, VAL1, VAL0, RND1, RND0]\n\ncolumns:\n  - name: STUDYID\n    type: str\n    label: Study Identifier\n    derivation: SOURCE.STUDYID\n\n  - name: USUBJID\n    type: str\n    label: Unique Subject Identifier\n    derivation: SOURCE.USUBJID\n\n  - name: VAL1\n    type: float\n    label: Source Value for One-Decimal Rounding\n    derivation: SOURCE.VAL1\n\n  - name: VAL0\n    type: float\n    label: Source Value for Whole-Number Rounding\n    derivation: SOURCE.VAL0\n\n  # FORMULA-16: exact ties and near ties below them move away from zero.\n  - name: RND1\n    type: float\n    label: Value Rounded to One Decimal Place\n    derivation:\n      round_half_away_from_zero:\n        source: VAL1\n        digits: 1\n\n  - name: RND0\n    type: float\n    label: Value Rounded to a Whole Number\n    derivation:\n      round_half_away_from_zero:\n        source: VAL0\n        digits: 0\n",
    "negative": "yamaa: \"1.0\"\ntype: spec\nmodel: ADaM\ndomain: ADSL\nkeys: [STUDYID, USUBJID]\ninput:\n  DM: input/dm.csv\n\noutput:\n  path: adsl.csv\n  columns: [STUDYID, USUBJID, RNDVAL]\n\ncolumns:\n  - name: STUDYID\n    type: str\n    label: Study Identifier\n    derivation: DM.STUDYID\n\n  - name: USUBJID\n    type: str\n    label: Unique Subject Identifier\n    derivation: DM.USUBJID\n\n  - name: SEX\n    type: str\n    label: Sex\n    derivation: DM.SEX\n\n  # The defect: SEX is a text code, and rounding accepts only a numeric\n  # source, so the specification is rejected before any data is read.\n  - name: RNDVAL\n    type: float\n    label: Rounded Value\n    derivation:\n      round_half_away_from_zero:\n        source: SEX\n        digits: 1\n",
    "adsl": "STUDYID,USUBJID,VAL1,VAL0\nYAMAA-01,YAMAA-01-001,2.45,\nYAMAA-01,YAMAA-01-002,-2.45,\nYAMAA-01,YAMAA-01-003,2.41,\nYAMAA-01,YAMAA-01-004,2.449999999,\nYAMAA-01,YAMAA-01-005,2.44999999,\nYAMAA-01,YAMAA-01-006,-2.449999999,\nYAMAA-01,YAMAA-01-007,-2.44999999,\nYAMAA-01,YAMAA-01-008,-0.04,\nYAMAA-01,YAMAA-01-009,,\nYAMAA-01,YAMAA-01-010,,2.5\nYAMAA-01,YAMAA-01-011,,-2.5\nYAMAA-01,YAMAA-01-012,,2.4\nYAMAA-01,YAMAA-01-013,,2.4999999999\nYAMAA-01,YAMAA-01-014,,2.4999999\nYAMAA-01,YAMAA-01-015,,-2.4999999999\nYAMAA-01,YAMAA-01-016,,-0.4\n"
  },
